{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide","id":960448,"title":"Nightmare, Dementation, Auspex, and suicide.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T08:17:32-07:00","id":960448,"title":"Nightmare, Dementation, Auspex, and suicide.","content":"I really only have experiance reading vtr, but I was on the vtm wiki reading about Malkavians and how they can make people suicidal. Nghtmare says it cant do this, while at the same time seeming suited to it. Auspex can implant memories, but didnt mention suicide. Is there a way to do this in vtr?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T08:29:16-07:00","id":960453,"title":"","content":"The Children of Judas bloodline have a special Discipline devoted to it, called <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Despond\" target=\"_blank\">Despond</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:41:34-07:00","id":960504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide#post960448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to do this in vtr?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meticulously find at least two things the person cares about and destroy all but one. - OR - If they care about nothing, cultivate two or more things of value (people, places, ideas) and slowly invest them into those creations. Attach their sense of self and identity (especially if you can use the Vinculum) to those things of value. Destroy all but one. Give them a second hope with another new thing and just before they commit to hope, destroy that too. For better results, manipulate them into destroying said things themselves, or frame it to appear like their intervention / hope brought the destruction about.<br /> <br /> Lay it all at their feet and then reveal the true darkness of the world itself, how monsters have claimed the mantle of the Divine, that governments are controlled by shadowy conspiracies, that there is no universal peace, justice or morality to hold out hope for.<br /> <br /> Threaten to destroy the last thing they value in the world - unless they martyr themselves. Either willingly, out of sheer despair, or by setting up a scenario where they think the only way to save this thing is by sacrificing themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 08-30-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:14:16-07:00","id":960521,"title":"","content":"Another way, is make a deal with a mage with Mind 2 (Mage 2ed).<br /> He will implant the suicide command for the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:54:30-07:00","id":960546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960453#post960453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Children of Judas bloodline have a special Discipline devoted to it, called <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Despond&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Despond</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despond had a reputation for being &quot;the suicide power&quot; because of the Bloodline it was associated with, but really it only had one ability that could actually make someone suicidal who wasn't already on the cusp. And even that didn't actually force them to kill themselves, it just gave them an extra Vice for taking self-destructive or dangerous actions. It was more like &quot;the depression power&quot;, giving people who were already seceptible an extra little push.<br /> <br /> They are hands down my favorite bloodline and I really want to write a 2e update for them. Maybe I'll take another crack at it when I have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:56:38-07:00","id":960547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960546#post960546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are hands down my favorite bloodline and I really want to write a 2e update for them. Maybe I'll take another crack at it when I have time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do I'd like to see it. Their theme seems like it would mix with the new bloodline power system well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:17:18-07:00","id":960558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960547#post960547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you do I'd like to see it. Their theme seems like it would mix with the new bloodline power system well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually thought it would be a good candidate for a Bloodline Discipline - dot 1 gives you a nightmare/majesty style aura of depression, dot 2 gives someone in the aura a Condition that makes them want to take dangerous risks, dot 3 lets you suggest a specific suicidal course of action to someone with the Condition, dot 4 lets you advance the Condition to a more extreme state... Not sure what to do about dot 5 yet, since in 1e it was basically just the postmortem embrace, which is a thing everyone can do for free now.<br /> <br /> I guess since the structure mirrors Majesty so closely, I could make it Majesty Devotions instead. I'll work on it a bit and see what comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T11:56:08-07:00","id":960579,"title":"","content":"Dominate 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:55:22-07:00","id":960653,"title":"","content":"There is nothing that says Dominate one wont work. Charmed says they will save their own skin, but dominate doesnt say that.<br /> <br /> I believe you could ask someone to &quot;Jump off the building&quot; or &quot;lay under that Bus&quot; or &quot;hold this&quot; - hand them a gun - &quot;Look at the barrel&quot; &quot;Pull the trigger&quot; That last one would take several turns. but it is entirely possible.<br /> <br /> Hand them a glass of bleach and tell them to drink it...<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: From what I understand, Comparing VTM and VTR is like comparing AD&amp;D to 5th Edtion (or even 3rd) and if you have never played DND, it's like apples and oranges.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-30-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:00:13-07:00","id":960656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960653#post960653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing that says Dominate one wont work. Charmed says they will save their own skin, but dominate doesnt say that. <br /> <br /> I believe you could ask someone to &amp;quot;Jump off the building&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;lay under that Bus&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;hold this&amp;quot; - hand them a gun - &amp;quot;Look at the barrel&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Pull the trigger&amp;quot; That last one would take several turns. but it is entirely possible. <br /> <br /> Hand them a glass of bleach and tell them to drink it...</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to dark delusions (nightmare dot 4 I think) could you make them believe their arm is a snake, so they might harm themselves, or believe they are on fire, while keeping an conviniant pool electified water nearby?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:19:37-07:00","id":960668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960656#post960656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to dark delusions (nightmare dot 4 I think) could you make them believe their arm is a snake, so they might harm themselves, or believe they are on fire, while keeping an conviniant pool electified water nearby?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely to the snake part, but you cant control what they do with that belief. They MIGHT cut their arm off, but I would assume as soon as they hurt themselves they might realize it's their arm and stop. ( disproving the illusion. ) Or they might think that was really cool and try to show their friends...<br /> <br /> Yes you could make them think they are on fire and they might stop drop and roll or go running for the water, but once they get a clear moment of thought and realize they dont hurt, they just might think they are the Human Torch. <br /> <br /> The Grand Delusion \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> The vampire defines his<br /> exact beliefs, but can\u2019t control his reaction to these beliefs,<br /> nor can she inspire a delusion that would make the victim<br /> homicidal or self-destructive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:22:06-07:00","id":960673,"title":"","content":"I agree with Vitalis. There was a long discussion about the fact if the breaking point would occurs before or after the suicidal act like pull the trigger or jump down the windows; for me it comes after. Anyway you could always say: &lt;&lt;close your eyes and jump backwards or cross the street &gt;&gt; while a bus is passing. In this way he wouldn't incurr in a breaking point anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-31-2016, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:28:12-07:00","id":960679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960668#post960668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Absolutely to the snake part, but you cant control what they do with that belief. They MIGHT cut their arm off, but I would assume as soon as they hurt themselves they might realize it's their arm and stop. ( disproving the illusion. ) Or they might think that was really cool and try to show their friends...<br /> <br /> Yes you could make them think they are on fire and they might stop drop and roll or go running for the water, but once they get a clear moment of thought and realize they dont hurt, they just might think they are the Human Torch. <br /> <br /> The Grand Delusion \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> The vampire defines his<br /> exact beliefs, but can\u2019t control his reaction to these beliefs,<br /> nor can she inspire a delusion that would make the victim<br /> homicidal or self-destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an example of how grand delusion don't work: something linked to someone covered by spiders if I remember well. And it say that just a look would disprove it. Bacteria otherwise....<br /> <br /> Anyway this could be something that could work with the forth power. And with dread presence can't be anything else but awful. So he wouldn't show to his friends thinking it's cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T14:33:30-07:00","id":960683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960673#post960673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Vitalis. There was a long discussion about the fact if the breaking point would occurs before or after the suicidal act like pull the trigger or jump down the windows; for me it comes after. Anyway you could always say: &gt; or while a bus is passing. In this way he wouldn't incurr in a breaking point anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the camp that says the Breaking point happens after. Something isnt Broken until After you break it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:28:42-07:00","id":960863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960558#post960558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually thought it would be a good candidate for a Bloodline Discipline - dot 1 gives you a nightmare/majesty style aura of depression, dot 2 gives someone in the aura a Condition that makes them want to take dangerous risks, dot 3 lets you suggest a specific suicidal course of action to someone with the Condition, dot 4 lets you advance the Condition to a more extreme state... Not sure what to do about dot 5 yet, since in 1e it was basically just the postmortem embrace, which is a thing everyone can do for free now.<br /> <br /> I guess since the structure mirrors Majesty so closely, I could make it Majesty Devotions instead. I'll work on it a bit and see what comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see what you were going for, but I think in the Devotion and theme system for bloodlines we've seen so far seems to obviate the need, for the most part, for Discipline dots that are required but only offer a minor and very narrow window for usage. Would the fourth dot offer anything more than an increase of the second dot's power? Is the third dot something you can't replicate socially or through other manipulations?<br /> <br /> A bad example, but what if the suicidal aura could have a seeping effect, stripping away the limits for Breaking Points through repeated exposure, or based upon contingencies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:03:40-07:00","id":963205,"title":"","content":"I don't know about a single use of a power, but yeah, I'd argue any repeated and clever use of an appropriate discipline could drive someone to suicide (or snapping and getting themselves killed). Nightmare, being all about exploiting the fears would easily drive someone nuts since no medication would help and suicide would be an easy way out. Dominating someone into doing stuff they don't remember (like antagonizing their loved ones or dominating the loved ones to do it) or messing with their memories could have the same outcome. Of course, the hard part is getting in touch with them regularly enough.<br /> <br /> Another really fucked up way to do this would be drugs. I say you can't dominate someone into doing something they realize could kill them, but dominate them (or push them with majesty, jesus, a drug dealer/pusher with majesty would be a nightmare) into putting needles into themselves, then dominate/majesty them into &quot;come on, I'm augmenting the dose this time, I want a bigger rush, you with me ?&quot;. Then, just don't call an ambulance when they OD. It's not exactly suicide, but the end result is pretty much the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T05:07:39-07:00","id":963635,"title":"","content":"Dominate can, but you need Dominate 2 and they need to fail a breaking point.<br /> <br /> I actually feel like Nightmare is a better model for a custom The Suicide Power. Not being able to spend willpower at the first dot is a good depression mechanic. The illusion / intimidate aspect is a bit off, but not completely. Second dot overwhelms them with depression so they cant do anything without spending a willpower. Third dot can catch people in the self destructive all-your-fault loop. Fourth doesn't particularly fit. Fifth can actually work almost as-is. Instead of supernatural signs of fear they get physical markings of self harm and a condition that encourages them to do more self harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:57:37-07:00","id":963673,"title":"","content":"Offhand. I'd make the Children of Judas unable to embrace *except* post mortums on suicides as their weakness, plus another small thing that makes them dependant on making people sad... maybe they lose the first (10-Humanity) Vitae they take from victims unless they are depressed, suffering from a persostent condition resulting from a breaking point, or engaged in self harm in the past 24hrs.<br /> <br /> Not sure on Gift. I tenatively want to do something that has to do with them feeding blood, possobly in the place of blood bonds.<br /> <br /> Make disciplines Auspex, Despond, Resilience, Vigor. Upon joining the bloodline all Majesty dots convert to Despond dots. The character's dots in Celerity are traded for Resilience, and visa versa.<br /> <br /> As for Despond...<br /> <br /> Despond 1<br /> Aura. Can lash out to defend. People can't spend willpower on actions, but can on defenses. Failures become dramatic failures unless they spend a willpower. People take a penalty on all breaking point rolls equal to Despond dots. People in the aura gain Depression as a vice, which triggers if they inflict lethal damage<br /> <br /> Despond 2<br /> Overwhelm the target with sadness. They will cry and audibly lament about their hidden sorrows, which are magnified and brought to bare. The target gains the Insensate tilt, though they may engage in self harm unimpeded. Inflicting lethal damage on themselves ends the tilt. So long as the tilt lasts, if they do not spend willpower to do something else or engage in self harm, then they must talk about their greatest sources of sadness. The Child of Judas may guide the conversation to a specific sadness with a Manipulation + Empathy roll. The target will feel glad to have had someone to listen to them, and their impression of the vampire improves by one step. However, this doesn't cause the victim to trust the vampire, and they may regret their sharing the information and seek to contain it.<br /> <br /> Despond 3<br /> Give the target a Condition. Target becomes absolutely convinced that everyone hates them because they terrible and have done somethiing wrong and its all their fault. Friends arent just busy, they dont want to be near you because you are annoying. All rolls to interact with people socially are reduced to a chance die unless you spend willpower to enhance the diceroll. Empathy rolls are hampered even then, the willpower only allowing the roll instead of adding dice. The victim also may not recover willpower except through Despond. Whenever the victim's beliefs are validated or they engage in self destructive acts (doesnt have to be physical) they gain a point of willpower and a beat. Condition can be shed by suffering a dramatic failure on a breaking point. Otherwise it lasts for one night, or a number of days equal to the vampire's blood potency if Despond 1 is active.<br /> <br /> Despond 4<br /> Sap the target's energy. They suffer a condition that gives a -2 penalty to all rolls and they can not heal through any means. Any activity time the target makes a non-reflexive roll they take one bashing damage from the stress.<br /> <br /> Despond 5<br /> Target takes lethal damage, which manafests as sogns of self harm. The target gains the addicted condition towards taking damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:38:05-07:00","id":963710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=963635#post963635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate can, but you need Dominate 2 and they need to fail a breaking point.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question. Dominate 1 vs 2 they still do the same thing one is better as Iron Edict allows for longer commands that you can't go against sure. But why is handing someone a glass and telling them to &quot;drink it all&quot; not a valid command, just so happens the glass is full of bleach or arsenic or something. That is strictly in the area of Dominate 1. Or a syringe full of something, your command is &quot;Inject it all&quot; <br /> Even if you two were on a roof top and you told them to &quot;Jump down&quot; I still think they would do it. Or if you were in a boat and you told them to &quot;swim to shore&quot; Sure, shore is 4 miles away.... but still I think they would do it with Dominate 1.<br /> <br /> I am curious as to why you think that Dominate 2 is required as well as a failed breaking point. Thanks for the insight! <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:46:40-07:00","id":963786,"title":"","content":"Dominate 1 causes mesmirize, which breaks when they attempt a breaking point roll, pass or fail. Dominate 2 causes the Dominated condition, which only breaks if they succeed.<br /> <br /> If you make then kill themselves in a way that doesnt cause a breaking point then Dominate 1 works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:51:47-07:00","id":963793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=963710#post963710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. Dominate 1 vs 2 they still do the same thing one is better as Iron Edict allows for longer commands that you can't go against sure. But why is handing someone a glass and telling them to &amp;quot;drink it all&amp;quot; not a valid command, just so happens the glass is full of bleach or arsenic or something. That is strictly in the area of Dominate 1. Or a syringe full of something, your command is &amp;quot;Inject it all&amp;quot; <br /> Even if you two were on a roof top and you told them to &amp;quot;Jump down&amp;quot; I still think they would do it. Or if you were in a boat and you told them to &amp;quot;swim to shore&amp;quot; Sure, shore is 4 miles away.... but still I think they would do it with Dominate 1.<br /> <br /> I am curious as to why you think that Dominate 2 is required as well as a failed breaking point. Thanks for the insight!</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe SoulGambit is assuming that the subject attempting to kill themselves would count as a Breaking Point. At that point, it's a simple matter of the way the Conditions work. Mezmerized is resolved if the subject experiences a Breaking Point and Dominated is resolved if the subject experiences a Breaking Point and succeed the Resolve + Composure roll.<br /> <br /> I don't agree that any command that would lead to the subject's death if carried out would necessarily constitute a Breaking Point - it depends on the subject and the command. Your &quot;drink it all&quot; example probably wouldn't trigger a Breaking Point in my opinion, unless they knew it contained poison. &quot;Inject yourself with this&quot; might or might not, depending on how they feel about needles, and ditto &quot;swim to shore&quot; depending on how they feel about the ocean and &quot;jump down&quot; depending on how they feel about heights. But, &quot;shoot your own head&quot; probably would in most people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:49:45-07:00","id":963819,"title":"","content":"It was lightly touched on in this thread, and bringing it back might constitute as hijacking, but that does pose another question.<br /> <br /> &quot;Experience a breaking point as part of a vampire\u2019s command.&quot; &lt;- that is how you resolve the condition. How can you &quot;experience a breaking point&quot; without actually doing anything? Say shooting myself would be a breaking point, but how could I know that I have hit that breaking point without actually pulling the trigger? <br /> <br /> It would be like &quot;getting high&quot; as a breaking point, but unless I actually physically smoke the whatever I havent hit that breaking point. I could sit there with it in my hand, even put it to my mouth, and not experience the breaking point of &quot;getting high&quot; because I didnt actually do it. <br /> <br /> Or even if you take a glass plate. I think about dropping it and I know it will shatter, but it isnt actually going to get broken until someone drops it. Until the action of letting go has been done, the plate wont get break, and in some cases, the plate doesn't even break when it hits the ground.<br /> <br /> If you are afraid of heights to the point of it being a phobia, you probably werent on the roof to begin with, but how can you experience a breaking point from.. the POSSIBILITY of jumping? The breaking point would happen when you are falling, when you had already jumped. <br /> <br /> Dominate condition is better worded &quot;Experience a breaking point when following the command,&quot; So when you lift the gun to shoot yourself, but the time you &quot;experience the breaking point from following the command&quot; It would be too late. Your condition would be resolved, but you would also be dead/dying. Simply holding a gun shouldnt be a breaking point. Pulling the trigger should be. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:13:23-07:00","id":963905,"title":"","content":"Using Nightmare to drive someone to kill themselves is easy, just torment them continuously with it, then make it clear suicide is the only way to stop the misery. You won't compel them to commit suicide, eventually they'll make that choice for themselves. The question is how long do they last before they can endure no more. They have a choice nore suffering or suicide, given repeatedly until they chose suicide (or someone gives you the final death for being a sadistic fuck).<br /> <br /> Using magic to force someone to kill themselves isn't really suicide, suicide requires free will, using magic that strips that choice from them is just like if you grabbed thier hand beat them to death with their own hand, there is no choice to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T16:23:26-07:00","id":963965,"title":"","content":"*peeks into thread* Why would anyone want to magically compell someone to commit suicide? That's a terrible thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:01:28-07:00","id":964049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=963965#post963965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*peeks into thread* Why would anyone want to magically compell someone to commit suicide? That's a terrible thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are a primarily Lancea et Sanctum bloodline, and they kill people for the usual reasons the Lancea et Sanctum do. To punish those they perceive as deserving of punishment and to teach lessons to others. Then there's the other usual reasons vampires kill others, out of loneliness, because they need something a death would bring to them, sadistic entertainment and so on. Ego.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/18/1b/80/181b800f3c15f3d92efcb6e118f94921.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But to be fair, they don't only use magic to drive people to suicide, and are entirely capable of using mundane abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-06-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:17:26-07:00","id":967645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=960504#post960504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meticulously find at least two things the person cares about and destroy all but one. - OR - If they care about nothing, cultivate two or more things of value (people, places, ideas) and slowly invest them into those creations. Attach their sense of self and identity (especially if you can use the Vinculum) to those things of value. Destroy all but one. Give them a second hope with another new thing and just before they commit to hope, destroy that too. For better results, manipulate them into destroying said things themselves, or frame it to appear like their intervention / hope brought the destruction about.<br /> <br /> Lay it all at their feet and then reveal the true darkness of the world itself, how monsters have claimed the mantle of the Divine, that governments are controlled by shadowy conspiracies, that there is no universal peace, justice or morality to hold out hope for.<br /> <br /> Threaten to destroy the last thing they value in the world - unless they martyr themselves. Either willingly, out of sheer despair, or by setting up a scenario where they think the only way to save this thing is by sacrificing themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I should be distrubed by this.....even more so coming from someone using the ID &quot;Holy&quot;. Shame on you. :P<br /> <br /> Children of Judas should be restricted to only feeding on those that are depressed/suicidal. Which makes keeping a herd rather problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 09-11-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T18:28:38-07:00","id":967650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=967645#post967645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Children of Judas should be restricted to only feeding on those that are depressed/suicidal. Which makes keeping a herd rather problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that too limiting and that it doesn't really open up play the way causing suicide does. Besides, you can just use your powers to get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T17:57:44-07:00","id":968282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/960448-nightmare-dementation-auspex-and-suicide?p=967650#post967650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find that too limiting and that it doesn't really open up play the way causing suicide does. Besides, you can just use your powers to get them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I just like the idea of a vampire that has to feed of those with mental illness. A psyhic ward as a haven and feeding ground is an interesting concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}